## Context

[[0876]] has a remaining exit condition: no currency conversion embedded in
a script; a `rates` row must cite the line that reports the conversion. The
four-country Figure 1 script currently sets Senegal's USD package denominator
to `2500 * 1.09` at
`conception/jetp/papier-court-mesure/figure-distribution-decaissement.py:43`.
The 2,500 million euro package is labelled, but the `1.09` EUR-to-USD rate has
no date, basis or cited line there. `data/jetp/rates.csv` currently has only
its header. `docs/jetp-ledger-migration.md` already names this exact literal
as the one known inline exchange rate.

The figure divides CRS USD disbursement by that converted package amount, so
the conversion changes a plotted percentage. This is an analytical input,
not a formatting detail. The existing `rates` schema requires `currency`,
`date`, `basis`, `rate_to_usd`, `line_id` and `recorded_at`.

## Work

1. Identify the source and date/basis for the rate used in the comparison,
   and cite an exact ingested line. If no source supports `1.09`, replace it
   with a documented, source-backed conversion or withdraw the USD-normalized
   Senegal denominator until one exists; do not present `1.09` as sourced.
2. Move any accepted conversion into `data/jetp/rates.csv`; make the figure
   read the ledger rate by key and fail clearly when it is absent. Record the
   chosen date/basis and the effect on the plotted Senegal percentage.
3. Review the figure caption and provenance so a reader can follow the
   package amount and the conversion separately.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No literal FX multiplier remains in the figure script or its related
      analysis path.
- [ ] Every published conversion has a positive `rates.rate_to_usd`, date,
      basis and a `line_id` whose source states that rate or equivalent; if
      no such line exists, the figure visibly avoids the conversion.
- [ ] A focused test catches a missing or mismatched rate, the ledger check
      passes, and the changed figure is rebuilt and compared with its prior
      output; pipeline gates run per `AGENTS.md`.
